A measurement observes a filtered field (@mat-measurement-operator: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Additive-Manufacturing-Residual-Strain-AM-Bench.lingua#r_1JF3D3C7YNFKCJET729ADPZWPM", #source "../sources/Data-Evaluation-for-Materials-Properties-NIST.lingua#r_7N31EWH1JVE54EM3BRSQGYS04K", #materials-engineering "Identifiability-before-parameter-fitting.lingua#r_1A1YWQT30VVSZR0HJPZDX0TM9X", #clean-manufacturing "../../../production/clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control/surface-measurement/A-surface-measurement-has-spatial-and-depth-weighting.lingua#r_0R6W16HGTMM3XQ60ZB9K6NMBHJ") { r_4P5XG26ENMZPFN5ED5HXZRWCV7
**Read:** [Manufacturing history and measured residual strain — AM-Bench 2018](../sources/Additive-Manufacturing-Residual-Strain-AM-Bench.lingua#r_1JF3D3C7YNFKCJET729ADPZWPM), neutron measurement geometry and raw-table conventions; [Data Evaluation: Theory and Practice for Materials Properties — Ronald G. Munro](../sources/Data-Evaluation-for-Materials-Properties-NIST.lingua#r_7N31EWH1JVE54EM3BRSQGYS04K), measurement procedures. Return to diffraction, microscopy and continuum strain when needed.

A measurement is an operation on a specimen, not necessarily a field value at a point. A simple model is y=∫w(x)ε(x)dx+η, with normalized sensitivity w and measurement error η. Diffraction, image correlation, indentation and thermal measurements use different operators and may combine several physical effects. Predict the measured quantity through that operator before comparing it with a model field.

For a one-dimensional illustrative strain ε(x)=a+b cos(2πx/L), a uniform gauge of width g centered at x₀ returns a+b sinc(πg/L)cos(2πx₀/L), where sinc(z)=sin(z)/z and sinc(0)=1. A width g=L removes this entire oscillatory contribution. This deliberately simple example is not the full diffraction weighting of the NIST experiment.

**Work:** Derive the expression by integration and check g→0 and g=L. Numerically integrate several shifted gauges independently. Construct two distinct fields giving the same observation. For the AM data, identify the needed gauge geometry, coordinate transformation, reference spacing and diffraction-elastic interpretation before converting lattice strain into a stress claim.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
